## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a rectangular block with a front and back side) that flips around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Wrapper – gives perspective so the 3D effect looks good */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* how far the viewer is from the card */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – positioned relative so we can rotate it */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s;    /* smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Front & back faces – absolute positioning, backface hidden */
.card__face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when it’s turned away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* Front face – normal orientation */
.card__face--front {
  background: #3498db;          /* blue */
}

/* Back face – rotated 180° so it’s hidden initially */
.card__face--back {
  background: #e74c3c;          /* red */
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* 4️⃣  Hover effect – rotate the whole card 180° around Y */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives depth to the 3D transform. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` on faces | Hides the side that is turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the card around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

### Tweaks you might want

| Property | What it changes | Example |
|----------|-----------------|---------|
| `transition` | Speed of the flip | `transition: transform 0.4s;` |
| `perspective` | How “deep” the flip looks | `perspective: 800px;` |
| `rotateY` | Flip direction | `rotateY(-180deg)` for left‑to‑right flip |
| `border-radius` | Rounded corners | `border-radius: 20px;` |
| `box-shadow` | Depth effect | `box-shadow: 0 8px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.3);` |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the faces. Happy coding!
